    "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 12 at 8:19AM PDT until August 13 at 9:00PM PDT by NWS Reno NV",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of western Nevada, including the following area,\nGreater Reno-Carson City-Minden Area. This includes the Bug and\nStallion Fires.\n\n* WHEN...From 2 PM PDT this afternoon through Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in rock, mud, and debris\nflows in and near active fire perimeters, steep terrain, and poorly\ndrained urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Heavy rain from thunderstorms primarily during the afteroon and\nevening hours today and Thursday.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
